   "source": [
    "# Setting up CANFAR to read from Rubin ## \n",
    "\n",
    "The CANFAR version of the LSST Science Platform has some additional hooks designed to make working with Rubin data that are stored at the LSST site straightforward.  \n",
    "\n",
    "Users must first store a Rubin ACCESS TOKEN in a predefined location on CANFAR and then specify that they want to connect to RSP data sources (the default is to use data sources inside the CANFAR Science Platform, but not all LSST data products are stored inside CANFAR)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4f62f9f3-83aa-495a-85ce-aa9b8390bf90",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-06T05:38:32.308655Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-06T05:38:32.308191Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-06T05:38:32.316643Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-06T05:38:32.315534Z",
     "shell.execute_reply.started": "2026-11-06T05:38:32.308613Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "### Setting up an ACCESS TOKEN ###\n",
    "Import the canfar module that aids in retrieving and storing the Rubin ACCESS TOKEN\n",
    "and then login to RSP, get a token and store it in the pre-defined location"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "e345584e-a977-4b98-a80a-a440ea87f60a",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-06T05:41:25.903008Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-06T05:41:25.902485Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-06T05:41:25.910534Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-06T05:41:25.909157Z",
     "shell.execute_reply.started": "2026-11-06T05:41:25.902963Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from canfar_tokens import login_rubin, rubin_token\n",
    "# Uncomment the next line to actually do the login step (once per user token lifetime)\n",
    "# login_rubin()   # once; paste the token from https://data.lsst.cloud/settings/tokens\n",
    "access_token = rubin_token()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6cbf77d0-a347-42b7-a609-f1c24e7ce4b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Store the token as an environment variable (for Butler).\n",
    "Here we store the token value in a predefined environment variable that the Butler will use when accessing RSP store data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "1e578530-15b7-447f-96ff-dcee3df8e0f1",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-06T05:42:46.017831Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-06T05:42:46.017319Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-06T05:42:46.024400Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-06T05:42:46.022701Z",
     "shell.execute_reply.started": "2026-11-06T05:42:46.017785Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Butler doesn't have a token option, so we use an environment variable.\n",
    "import os\n",
    "os.environ[\"BUTLER_RUBIN_ACCESS_TOKEN\"] = access_token",
    "# The CANFAR version of Butler knows to look in BUTLER_RUBIN_ACCESS_TOKEN when making data requests to Rubin data.lsst.io.\n",
    "butler = Butler(\"rubin-dp2\", collections=[\"dp2\"])"

   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2111c333-8332-4fde-99fc-79416a6211b9",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-06T05:36:31.180158Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-06T05:36:31.179306Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-06T05:36:31.291615Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-06T05:36:31.290347Z",
     "shell.execute_reply.started": "2026-11-06T05:36:31.180102Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "### Use the access_token for data service access.\n",
    "\n",
    "Note that we use the access alias 'rubin-dp2' to indicate we want services provided by Rubin, instead of CANFAR.  If you want to use CANFAR's copy of the service, use the alias 'dp2'.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "158269b5-a897-4778-bc99-7990e55b7a4b",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-06T05:44:42.836935Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-06T05:44:42.836414Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-06T05:44:44.857469Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-06T05:44:44.854789Z",
     "shell.execute_reply.started": "2026-11-06T05:44:42.836889Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from lsst.rsp import RSPDiscovery\n",
    "from lsst.daf.butler import Butler\n",
    "# Note that 'access_token' defined above is passed to the RSPDiscovery service so it knows to use that token for access.\n",
    "discovery = RSPDiscovery(\"rubin-dp2\", token=access_token)\n",
    "service = discovery.get_tap_client()\n",
   ]
  },
